  "body": "## CamCraft 0.19.0\n\nA minor release: wire EDM and sinker EDM, more turning, new posts (grblHAL, TinyG, generic ISO wire and sinker EDM), a much larger MCP surface, stricter STEP verification. 237 pull requests merged since 0.18.0; the full notes are in `RELEASE_NOTES.md`, 179+ rows in `CHANGELOG.md`, 185 decision files gathered into `RECOMMENDED.md`.\n\n### Breaking\n- Thread milling reworked (issue 894, PR 1005): thread mills are tool kinds, the Thread operation cuts by helical interpolation, and it no longer accepts a Tap-kind tool.\n- The document's unit is the unit every post writes (issue 902, PR 981); Carvera, Heidenhain and Fanuc Lathe refuse an inch document by name.\n- Air coolant and machine default coolant (issue 869, PR 961).\n- Project file format v59 (issue 1056, PR 1341): older projects open with models marked \"fidelity unknown\" until re-imported.\n\n### Not exercised on a real control\n- Generic ISO wire EDM post and generic ISO sinker EDM post (synthetic, codes are machine data).\n- Wire taper, tabs, no-core burnout and 4-axis wire as merged; sinker orbit, side burn and wear moves.\n- Turning thread infeed plan (issue 516).\n- Rotary feed cap (PR 1395) and Doosan DNM A-state (PR 1396): merged without a PathPilot Hub run.\n- grblHAL and TinyG posts; thread milling verified in simulation only.\n\n### Process changes\nPROCESS_VERSION 16 to 54 since v0.18.0 (23 and 27 were not announced), from pinned issue 681: 17 gh-issues skill; MCP skill rows (18, 20, 22, 25, 28, 34, 35, 40, 41, 43-53); gate maps and moved test suites (19, 21, 33, 37, 38, 42); icons tooling (24, 26); P1-P9 priorities (29); gate VOID report (30); refresh only at merge time and collaborator reviews (31, 32); placement rules and the UI AGENTS.md (36, 39); cut step 5 (54).\n\n### Gate\n`cargo xtask release --version 0.19.0 --no-tag --installer`, logs in `gate-logs/release-20261113-143242`: all 14 lanes ok, 0 failed, 50.5 min. The three UI snapshot goldens (egui_app, egui_app_light, egui_tool_editor) were regenerated at the cut after the maintainer's look.\nArtifact: `dist/camcraft-0.19.0-win-x64.zip` (33,168,163 bytes). No installer: Inno Setup is not installed on the cut machine, so the zip is the release; the published artifact is built by the release workflow from the tag. Binaries are unsigned.\n\nNot merged and not tagged by this PR's author. After the merge: confirm `git diff <branch tip> main` is empty, then tag the merge commit.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
